WEBVTT

00:05.630 --> 00:08.299
I quit. This is ridiculous.

00:09.759 --> 00:11.428
Yukino, wait!

00:11.511 --> 00:15.098
I joined the Rangers to fight monsters.

00:15.181 --> 00:17.434
I didn't hear anything about
fighting those guys!

00:17.517 --> 00:20.061
And if you're going to keep running away
like you did today,

00:20.145 --> 00:22.272
it'll be more efficient to quit now.

00:22.355 --> 00:24.441
Yukino.

00:27.777 --> 00:28.862
Usukubo!

00:28.945 --> 00:33.116
Oh, sorry...
I guess the nerves finally wore off.

00:33.199 --> 00:35.118
And this is just the first day...

00:35.201 --> 00:37.162
We still have to do this
for two more days?

00:39.080 --> 00:42.375
Just run back home
if you're scared, weaklings.

00:42.459 --> 00:45.295
Your willpower is admirable,
I'll give you that.

00:45.378 --> 00:48.882
In any case, the reckless way you fought
saved me back there.

00:48.965 --> 00:53.219
I'll continue to count on you tomorrow.
Let's both make our dreams come true.

00:54.471 --> 00:56.264
Who's a weakling?

00:56.347 --> 00:59.768
That tiny female Ranger...
For how she looks, she's monstrous!

01:00.477 --> 01:01.478
Damn it!

01:01.561 --> 01:02.562
Eigen...

01:02.645 --> 01:05.106
I didn't say I'm giving up!

01:05.190 --> 01:08.610
Let's go, Ranmaru.
We'll do a strategy meeting for tomorrow.

01:08.693 --> 01:09.694
G-Got it!

01:11.863 --> 01:14.532
Those two are always together.

01:14.616 --> 01:16.910
I heard they're childhood friends.

01:16.993 --> 01:17.994
How's Pink Squad doing?

01:18.078 --> 01:19.621
Nope, not good!

01:19.704 --> 01:21.498
Shippou said he lacked training,

01:21.581 --> 01:23.416
so he cooped himself up
in the training room.

01:23.500 --> 01:27.170
Is that so? I knew it, those proctors...

01:29.255 --> 01:32.425
<i>They have no intention of letting us pass.</i>

01:36.805 --> 01:38.932
- That moron!
- What's wrong, Hibiki?

01:39.015 --> 01:42.102
Oh, man! Now I feel like training too!

01:42.185 --> 01:43.269
All right!

01:43.353 --> 01:44.354
Hey, Sakurama.

01:44.437 --> 01:46.231
Huh? What is it?

01:47.607 --> 01:49.025
I'm in a rush here!

01:51.736 --> 01:53.655
We need to talk. Come with me.

01:53.738 --> 01:57.117
I told you I'm in a rush!
Let's talk later!

01:57.867 --> 01:58.868
Tsk.

02:10.964 --> 02:12.298
Hey!

02:12.799 --> 02:14.551
Get back to the stronghold now!

02:14.634 --> 02:16.845
This dusty hole
ain't no stronghold of mine--

02:28.606 --> 02:30.441
Go! Go! Loser Ranger!

03:54.275 --> 03:55.276
Episode 7
The Zigzag Road to the Final Exam!

03:55.360 --> 03:59.822
Sorry to keep you waiting.
What did you want to talk about?

03:59.906 --> 04:03.201
Sakurama.
Why did you join the Rangers?

04:03.284 --> 04:06.204
What's your intention
behind that question?

04:06.287 --> 04:10.208
The you spouting naive crap
about reconciling with monsters,

04:10.291 --> 04:12.293
and the you I saw during the exam...

04:12.377 --> 04:14.212
Which is the real you?

04:17.090 --> 04:20.969
I need to know what you really think
in order to work together tomorrow.

04:24.055 --> 04:26.975
<i>Time's up!
The first day of the final exam ends here!</i>

04:27.058 --> 04:30.770
This voice... Is it from that thing?
That scared the hell out of me.

04:30.853 --> 04:31.854
Take this!
- Huh?

04:31.938 --> 04:35.233
Ain't no way we're stopping when things
are getting this exciting, right?

04:35.316 --> 04:37.443
Let's go into added time!

04:38.945 --> 04:42.365
We're still a team despite how he acts,
so I can't overlook this.

04:42.448 --> 04:43.866
Team?

04:44.450 --> 04:46.369
You're still having that misconception?

04:46.452 --> 04:47.870
What?
Sakurama!

04:47.954 --> 04:50.873
Look at the belt wrapped behind him!
The key's right there!

04:50.957 --> 04:52.000
What?

04:52.583 --> 04:53.668
Huh?

04:56.045 --> 04:58.131
How long are you guys gonna keep this up?

04:59.090 --> 05:02.093
Tsk. Remember this, Hisui.

05:02.176 --> 05:06.014
Jeez, it's over already.
Stop harping on it, will you?

05:07.223 --> 05:10.476
<i>Could it be...
There was only one key.</i>

05:11.060 --> 05:14.897
<i>Assuming Tokita's speaking the truth,
each person needs a key.</i>

05:15.398 --> 05:18.067
<i>It's a battle between two people
from the same squad.</i>

05:18.151 --> 05:19.652
<i>This is the true nature of this exam.</i>

05:20.278 --> 05:23.239
<i>It's devised such that either Shion or I
will fail the exam.</i>

05:23.823 --> 05:28.786
<i>Shion... For the sake of us monsters,
I'll end your dream here.</i>

05:35.585 --> 05:37.253
This is horrible.

05:37.337 --> 05:39.505
Forget repairing,
I'll need to replace the entire thing.

05:39.589 --> 05:41.507
Here we go.

05:41.591 --> 05:44.552
- Uh...
- Wait, why's there a girl here?

05:49.599 --> 05:50.767
That surprised me.

05:50.850 --> 05:54.062
Why is there a Duster in Sakurama's room?

05:58.399 --> 06:01.319
Be good and don't put up a fight.

06:01.402 --> 06:03.321
It'll be disastrous
if this causes a ruckus.

06:03.404 --> 06:05.239
<i>Not good.
I'm gonna be killed!</i>

06:06.407 --> 06:09.327
I'll let you escape, so please be quiet.

06:09.410 --> 06:13.831
Wh-What are you saying?
Is this a trap? I won't be fooled!

06:15.166 --> 06:17.085
You don't have to be so on guard.

06:17.168 --> 06:21.381
I may have joined the Rangers,
but I don't really like to fight.

06:21.464 --> 06:22.465
Uh...

06:22.548 --> 06:26.219
That's why I undertake
the maintenance position underground.

06:26.302 --> 06:30.473
It's just my ego talking here.
You won't kill me.

06:30.556 --> 06:32.725
I don't want to kill you.

06:34.519 --> 06:36.062
13 years ago,

06:36.145 --> 06:37.772
my older sister and I were in danger

06:37.855 --> 06:39.816
when a monster
by the name of God attacked us,

06:39.899 --> 06:41.943
and Blue Keeper saved us.

06:43.653 --> 06:46.072
I admired him,
so I wanted to join the Rangers--

06:46.155 --> 06:47.240
Is that true?

06:47.323 --> 06:48.324
What?

06:48.408 --> 06:52.453
Tell me more about that God monster.
<i>Not good!</i>

06:52.537 --> 06:56.290
I-I don't really know,
since everything happened in an instant.

06:56.374 --> 06:58.292
It's probably one of the boss monsters.

06:58.793 --> 07:00.795
I guessed as much.

07:01.712 --> 07:03.464
I've got a score to settle with them too.

07:04.549 --> 07:08.678
They killed my older brother.
I swear I'll find them.

07:10.430 --> 07:12.682
<i>Although my brother was a Ranger,</i>

07:12.765 --> 07:14.225
<i>the brutality of boss monsters</i>

07:14.308 --> 07:16.978
<i>are on a completely different level
compared to the Dusters.</i>

07:17.061 --> 07:18.729
<i>There was nothing I could do.</i>

07:19.814 --> 07:24.318
<i>All I could do was watch
as my brother got trampled on.</i>

07:25.069 --> 07:27.488
<i>There was nothing I could do but watch.</i>

07:28.281 --> 07:30.783
<i>But I'm completely different
from back then.</i>

07:30.867 --> 07:34.871
No matter who my opponent is,
I will bury them with my own hands.

07:34.954 --> 07:38.875
<i>Now I get
why this dude just charges recklessly.</i>

07:38.958 --> 07:42.628
<i>The desire for revenge.
So that's the root of it all.</i>

07:42.712 --> 07:46.466
<i>I know very well
how such motivation gives you strength.</i>

07:46.549 --> 07:49.886
<i>I have to stop him here,
even if it means taking some risks.</i>

07:49.969 --> 07:52.430
But wouldn't that boss monster
be dead now?

07:52.513 --> 07:53.514
What?

07:53.598 --> 07:56.184
Didn't that happen a long time ago?

07:56.267 --> 07:57.768
If you haven't been able to find it,

07:57.852 --> 07:59.187
then isn't there a chance

07:59.270 --> 08:01.397
that the Dragon Keepers
already defeated it?

08:01.481 --> 08:04.650
<i>There's no record of them
appearing in Sunday Showdowns.</i>

08:05.234 --> 08:08.905
<i>For some reason, only incompetent
boss monsters appear during those times.</i>

08:08.988 --> 08:10.239
<i>Well...</i>

08:10.323 --> 08:13.326
<i>Those are just fake boss monsters
we made using our mimicry technique.</i>

08:13.409 --> 08:16.454
I need them to be alive.

08:16.537 --> 08:18.080
The only reason I'm alive now is because

08:18.164 --> 08:20.833
I'm trying to clear my brother's name
for the past four years.

08:20.917 --> 08:22.960
Four years?

08:23.044 --> 08:26.088
Didn't your older brother die
13 years ago?

08:26.172 --> 08:27.965
No, it was four years ago.

08:28.049 --> 08:29.592
But that's impossible!

08:29.675 --> 08:33.721
I mean, the boss monsters...
This has got to be a mistake...

08:34.680 --> 08:37.725
You're saying the same thing
as the Rangers.

08:37.808 --> 08:40.645
There was no evidence
that a boss monster was at the scene,

08:40.728 --> 08:43.189
so they didn't believe my testimony.

08:43.689 --> 08:46.192
No way. It can't be...

08:46.692 --> 08:51.197
<i>I don't get it. Is it possible
that a boss monster could be alive?</i>

08:52.323 --> 08:55.493
<i>XX... Do you know anything about this?</i>

08:56.577 --> 08:59.497
Let's search for a way to settle this
without fighting.

09:00.248 --> 09:04.835
I... I... I...

09:12.718 --> 09:14.262
H-How...

09:14.971 --> 09:18.516
Why are you here... Lord Peltrola?

09:22.937 --> 09:25.356
What? "Why," you ask?

09:25.439 --> 09:30.861
Weren't you the one who sent
a distress signal through this pipe, XX?

09:30.945 --> 09:32.405
S-Still,

09:32.488 --> 09:35.866
I could have just left by myself
if an escape route had been secured...

09:35.950 --> 09:38.494
What? You don't like this?

09:39.787 --> 09:40.788
N-Not at all!

09:40.871 --> 09:42.790
It is truly a great honor
for a boss monster

09:42.873 --> 09:44.250
to come get me personally!

09:44.333 --> 09:46.377
Hmm...

09:46.460 --> 09:52.758
Dear me, how pitiful... You're trembling.
You must have suffered.

09:52.842 --> 09:58.389
To think that my lovely XX
had been locked up in a place like this...

09:58.472 --> 10:01.392
Before He died and ascended to heaven,

10:01.475 --> 10:04.895
He left behind a wise saying
that I deeply resonate with.

10:04.979 --> 10:10.192
War is tragic.
It should not exist in this world.

10:10.776 --> 10:16.907
I wish for a peaceful world where
we do not have to resort to violent means.

10:16.991 --> 10:20.786
<i>Fighter D, you have to undo
your mimicry and escape now!</i>

10:20.870 --> 10:23.914
<i>At this rate, you'll be in danger too!</i>

10:24.790 --> 10:27.668
If I pass, he'll fail?

10:27.752 --> 10:32.506
All I could do was watch
as my brother got trampled on.

10:35.343 --> 10:37.553
This is getting more and more exciting!

10:38.137 --> 10:41.974
Will I be able to see how he looks
as I betray him at the very last minute?

10:42.058 --> 10:43.476
He'll be all like, "You coward!"

10:43.559 --> 10:46.228
Isn't that funny, XX?

10:46.812 --> 10:48.064
Huh?

10:48.648 --> 10:51.192
Come on, don't be put off.
We're monsters.

10:58.074 --> 11:01.827
He's late!
We're way past the starting time!

11:01.911 --> 11:03.746
Is that it? Is he using the toilet?

11:03.829 --> 11:04.830
Huh?

11:10.211 --> 11:11.212
<i>What?</i>

11:14.548 --> 11:15.549
Huh?

11:15.633 --> 11:19.428
Oh my, Koguma. Did they get you already?

11:19.512 --> 11:23.182
So you're the one from Red Squad
that Hisui mentioned?

11:24.308 --> 11:26.686
- Huh?
- No need to put up a guard around me.

11:26.769 --> 11:28.813
The rules state that monster actors

11:28.896 --> 11:30.940
who got their key taken
cannot fight anymore.

11:31.023 --> 11:32.024
What?

11:32.108 --> 11:35.945
Does that mean that the battle
within Blue Squad has finished?

11:41.534 --> 11:43.661
So what happened to Blue Squad?

11:43.744 --> 11:47.331
Well, I got done in
by the cadets' teamwork!

11:47.415 --> 11:48.958
That was well played!

11:49.041 --> 11:54.046
We never had anyone pass this exam
every year, but I think this is the year!

11:54.130 --> 11:57.383
This takes me back! When I was young...

11:57.466 --> 12:00.761
Sorry, but if you're just gonna chit-chat,
can we do it after the exam?

12:00.845 --> 12:04.890
Huh? I thought you're free
since your partner bailed on you.

12:04.974 --> 12:08.018
He didn't bail on me.
He'll come, I'm sure of it.

12:09.478 --> 12:10.479
Right.

12:10.563 --> 12:12.690
If you two don't work together,

12:12.815 --> 12:14.650
you won't be able to defeat
the monster actor.

12:14.734 --> 12:16.444
Forget about that already.

12:16.527 --> 12:18.738
Oh, so you've noticed already?

12:18.821 --> 12:23.701
Honestly, this is mean.
You just want us to destroy each other.

12:24.285 --> 12:27.705
What's this?
Are you hesitant to fight Shion?

12:27.788 --> 12:29.999
He's your friend?

12:30.082 --> 12:31.083
What?

12:31.167 --> 12:36.005
What? <i>Ore?</i> I mean, <i>boku?</i> No way!

12:36.088 --> 12:39.759
I-It's just that we've built up trust
on the first day.

12:39.842 --> 12:42.636
I know that we can defeat
the monster actor if we work together.

12:42.720 --> 12:45.139
After we work together to grab the key,

12:45.222 --> 12:48.976
I'll just cook up some convenient excuse
and go into hiding.

12:49.477 --> 12:51.228
Aww, I pity him.

12:51.312 --> 12:53.814
Unlike you guys,
I'm desperate.

12:53.898 --> 12:57.318
I'm also not like my peers, who love to
pretend play as allies of justice.

12:57.401 --> 12:58.736
I'm the only one.

12:58.819 --> 13:01.572
The only one who's fighting
with my life on the line.

13:01.655 --> 13:03.365
<i>What I do will directly affect</i>

13:03.449 --> 13:05.659
<i>the future of my comrades
back at the fortress.</i>

13:06.660 --> 13:08.829
<i>As if I'm stopping
because of some cheap sympathy.</i>

13:10.831 --> 13:14.168
If that's what you intend to do,
I guess I can help you.

13:14.251 --> 13:16.337
What?
Here's a big hint for you!

13:16.420 --> 13:18.380
I saw Tokita over there.

13:18.839 --> 13:20.925
And your friend too!

13:24.970 --> 13:28.474
H-Hey, Shion! You're jumping the gun!

13:28.557 --> 13:30.226
Are you listening?

13:30.810 --> 13:32.478
You can't do this alone!

13:35.564 --> 13:36.565
Dang.

13:44.615 --> 13:45.783
Crap.

13:48.828 --> 13:52.122
That hurt! There's five of us,
and we only barely managed to do it?

13:52.206 --> 13:55.501
But with this,
we got Red's key.

13:55.584 --> 13:57.127
All right.
- Three more left.

13:57.211 --> 14:00.130
Shion. What's the meaning of this?

14:00.214 --> 14:02.550
It's as you can see, Sakurama.

14:02.633 --> 14:05.886
This exam is a battle of keys
within the same squad.

14:05.970 --> 14:09.640
I'm teaming up with these guys.
From here on, you and I will part ways.

14:09.723 --> 14:12.893
I'm not giving up my seat
as an official Ranger, no matter what.

14:12.977 --> 14:15.896
You... coward!

14:15.980 --> 14:18.649
Hah! You still don't see it, do you?

14:18.732 --> 14:20.985
That's why you're such a simpleton.

14:21.068 --> 14:23.571
You're not allowed to lose
even once to the monsters.

14:23.654 --> 14:27.157
The day the Rangers lose
is when humanity comes to an end.

14:27.241 --> 14:28.742
<i>That's why we don't hold back</i>

14:28.826 --> 14:30.911
<i>and send the Dragon Keepers
to the frontlines.</i>

14:30.995 --> 14:34.331
They're the five strongest Rangers
from each of our squadrons.

14:34.832 --> 14:37.918
This exam is just like a Sunday Showdown.

14:41.505 --> 14:44.008
Be careful, Sakurama.

14:44.091 --> 14:46.677
The guys around you
are way, way more desperate

14:46.760 --> 14:48.762
than you think they are.

14:50.097 --> 14:51.181
I see.

14:51.265 --> 14:53.601
So you guys were abandoned too.

14:53.684 --> 14:55.895
I've been nothing but a burden to Ishikawa

14:55.978 --> 14:58.939
ever since the final exam started, anyway.

14:59.023 --> 15:00.858
I'm shocked, but I can understand why.

15:02.151 --> 15:04.278
Still, it's unforgivable.

15:05.487 --> 15:07.531
<i>That's right,
it's unforgivable.</i>

15:07.615 --> 15:09.617
<i>Screw you, Shion.</i>

15:09.700 --> 15:15.456
<i>It's okay for me to betray you,
but if you betray me, you're guilty.</i>

15:16.040 --> 15:17.249
Shall we team up too?

15:17.333 --> 15:18.334
- What?
- What?

15:18.417 --> 15:21.211
We're allowed to take keys
that have been taken, right?

15:21.295 --> 15:22.630
In that case...

15:25.007 --> 15:26.634
<i>Now that's interesting.</i>

15:30.846 --> 15:31.847
Koguma!

15:31.931 --> 15:35.851
The exam isn't over yet! Let's try again!

15:37.227 --> 15:38.354
It's impossible.

15:38.437 --> 15:41.440
Those five have the highest scores
among us during the training period.

15:41.523 --> 15:44.109
There's no way we can win
even if we join forces.

15:44.193 --> 15:46.445
<i>Dang. Seriously, this guy!</i>

15:47.613 --> 15:51.492
Why are you being all dejected?
You've only lost once...

15:51.575 --> 15:53.243
What do you know?

15:58.749 --> 16:00.501
On the contrary...

16:00.584 --> 16:03.504
Is there anyone else
who'd know that more than I do?

16:03.587 --> 16:07.508
Let's work together as fellow losers.

16:07.591 --> 16:12.262
Yeah... You're right.

16:12.346 --> 16:13.514
Sakurama!

16:13.597 --> 16:16.016
The other team has already gotten into
their fourth battle!

16:16.600 --> 16:18.519
What colors were
the third and fourth battles?

16:18.602 --> 16:19.812
Pink...

16:20.312 --> 16:21.355
...and Green.

16:21.855 --> 16:23.357
So the remaining one is...

16:24.274 --> 16:26.068
<i>Yellow's monster actor.</i>

16:27.611 --> 16:28.696
Hmm...

16:29.279 --> 16:32.449
One, two, three... Huh?

16:32.533 --> 16:36.704
That's all? I heard
that the other team has five members.

16:36.787 --> 16:39.581
C-Can't we just form a team of three?

16:40.708 --> 16:43.460
Well, I guess it's fine with you around.

16:43.544 --> 16:46.505
You've been
acting strange lately, Sakurama.

16:46.588 --> 16:47.840
What's wrong?

16:47.923 --> 16:50.801
You were being so cautious
around me the other day.

16:52.302 --> 16:53.721
I felt so sad.

16:53.804 --> 16:57.182
Th-Thank you for your concern.

16:57.266 --> 17:00.352
So, will you give me your key?

17:02.062 --> 17:06.483
This is an exam.
You think I'd hand it over that easily?

17:06.567 --> 17:08.193
Now that's a shame.

17:08.277 --> 17:11.071
You wouldn't be getting hurt
if you'd just hand it over quietly!

17:11.155 --> 17:13.323
That's what a bad guy would say!

17:13.407 --> 17:15.826
I guess we're really doing this, Hibiki!

17:24.668 --> 17:25.669
Dang.

17:32.384 --> 17:35.304
- A direct hit!
- Nice, Koguma!

17:35.387 --> 17:37.806
That's why I said it's not gonna work!

17:37.890 --> 17:42.227
You know, isn't it cheating to gang up
and beat up one person?

17:42.311 --> 17:44.772
Who's the one cheating here?

17:47.107 --> 17:49.026
A toy like that won't work on me.

17:49.109 --> 17:51.278
Didn't you hear about this from that boy?

17:51.361 --> 17:53.822
I knew it. She's monstrous!

18:02.498 --> 18:04.875
How much longer until the second day ends?

18:04.958 --> 18:06.293
There's five minutes left!

18:13.217 --> 18:15.594
It's boring when you use
the same attacks over and over.

18:15.677 --> 18:17.096
I'm tired of this.

18:17.930 --> 18:19.139
Time for our last resort!

18:19.223 --> 18:21.141
Right! That's our only hope!

18:27.397 --> 18:28.440
Nice try!

18:28.524 --> 18:31.693
But as for you... You're no good.

18:33.779 --> 18:36.115
- Yamato!
- I've been watching you.

18:36.198 --> 18:37.783
Did you think that you won't be targeted

18:37.866 --> 18:39.993
since you're standing
right behind everyone else?

18:40.536 --> 18:45.707
That's why your female partner yesterday
talked trash about you, you know?

18:46.875 --> 18:48.377
Did you forget?

18:48.460 --> 18:53.298
You're timid, cowardly,
and not suited to be a hero of justice.

19:00.639 --> 19:02.015
Hibiki!

19:02.099 --> 19:05.060
Suzukiri, I don't know
how you think a hero should act.

19:05.644 --> 19:08.063
But surprisingly,
it seems like anyone can become one.

19:08.647 --> 19:11.066
Even if they're a really bad guy.

19:12.151 --> 19:13.193
I see.

19:13.277 --> 19:14.945
Watch out, Hibiki!

19:15.779 --> 19:17.698
In that case, you can have it.
Here you go.

19:17.781 --> 19:19.199
- Huh?
- W-Woah!

19:19.283 --> 19:20.450
What?

19:20.534 --> 19:21.785
B-But why?

19:21.869 --> 19:24.705
Since you say
anyone can become a Dragon Keeper,

19:24.788 --> 19:28.709
it'll be more interesting
to let someone like you become one.

19:28.792 --> 19:30.961
<i>Now that's just complete nonsense...</i>

19:31.712 --> 19:33.463
Answer me this.

19:33.547 --> 19:36.967
What will you guys do
if you become official Rangers?

19:37.676 --> 19:38.677
I...

19:39.303 --> 19:40.888
I guess it'll be world domination...

19:40.971 --> 19:41.972
- What?
- Huh?

19:44.141 --> 19:46.977
You're really the best.
I'll be cheering you on.

19:47.561 --> 19:48.729
Well then, see you!

19:54.067 --> 19:59.364
Four more left.
You can do it, Fighter-kun.

20:00.073 --> 20:01.491
Thanks, Hibiki!

20:02.618 --> 20:06.955
Compared to you, I... I'm ashamed of myself!

20:07.039 --> 20:11.126
It's too early to let down your guard.
We're just getting started.

20:11.210 --> 20:14.046
You mean Ishikawa, Shion,
and the others, right?

20:14.630 --> 20:16.798
What's so great about them?

20:16.882 --> 20:19.968
If the elite team is fashioned
after the Dragon Keepers,

20:20.052 --> 20:24.431
then this time, we're the monster actors,
the Nefarious Monster Army!

20:24.514 --> 20:25.933
Monsters, huh?

20:26.016 --> 20:27.684
I don't know how to think about this.

20:27.768 --> 20:30.312
I wouldn't want to go out of my way
to be hated by people.

20:30.395 --> 20:32.314
Snap...

20:32.397 --> 20:35.317
I-I'm sure
there's guys out there who love monsters!

20:35.400 --> 20:36.735
Nah, I don't think so.

20:36.818 --> 20:38.654
There are! I'm sure of it!

20:38.737 --> 20:41.323
Hey, is the ending bell
going to ring soon?

20:41.406 --> 20:42.824
Y-You're right.

20:43.659 --> 20:46.578
Tomorrow's the real battle.
Let's not talk about that now.

20:47.162 --> 20:48.914
Yes, you're right.

20:49.748 --> 20:52.834
We're all here because there's something
we want to achieve.

20:53.418 --> 20:56.255
Let's create a miracle
and make our dreams come true.

20:56.338 --> 20:57.589
Mm.

20:59.591 --> 21:02.344
Hey, sorry to barge in
while you're all getting excited.

21:04.429 --> 21:05.597
What?

21:07.182 --> 21:08.225
Wha... Wait!

21:11.061 --> 21:12.354
G-Guys!

21:13.563 --> 21:18.110
You sure you guys aren't mistaken?
This isn't a match, but an exam.

21:18.193 --> 21:22.698
It's nothing but a rite of passage to show
who's on top, and who's at the bottom.

21:25.284 --> 21:28.787
Guys like you who rely on miracles
have no tomorrow.

21:31.832 --> 21:33.625
We win!

21:38.130 --> 21:40.173
Just how many inhumane exams

21:40.257 --> 21:43.885
and the likes have been conducted
at this place?

21:44.636 --> 21:46.638
I must grant them salvation.

23:29.908 --> 23:31.910
Translated by Qianni Lu

23:31.993 --> 23:33.495
I've got to hold it in.

23:33.578 --> 23:36.123
Huh? What's wrong, Fighter-kun?
Shout out loud!

23:36.206 --> 23:38.250
No, I have to hold myself back here.

23:38.333 --> 23:40.001
I said, shout out loud!

23:40.085 --> 23:42.170
<i>Next episode,
"Shout Out Loud, Cadets!"</i>

23:42.254 --> 23:44.965
- Do this properly!
- Ow! Wait, we already did this last week!

23:45.048 --> 23:46.925
This is what we call a "Tendon"!
